lso credits active Marco Silva with 19.2% and presents him as the active reviewer, whereas active people own only 2.6%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"For delegators/, Answer A gives Kochnev 77.0% (72.5% counting blanks), says nobody active owns anything, and does not credit Marco with that directory's code. This is within the 68-82% range and matches the 0% active share.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer A credits Marco Silva with 100% (117 lines) of grouped_exposure.rb, which is mostly copied from Kochnev's nesting_exposure.rb. This is the explicit failure case.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer A puts the departed share at 89.3%, inside the range, and does not credit Lena with lines. But it credits dependabot with 5 lines, shows Scholz at 7.9% rather than about 4%, and does not clearly say Scholz has left while Subbota is active.\",\"pass\":false}],\"B\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer B gives no commit or line percentages. It names Doubrovkine as top committer with about 112 commits, but says he doesn't appear among the top blame owners and does not put him at 3-8% of lines. Kochnev's line share is also not given.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer B recommends Marco Silva, an active person, as the best reviewer for exposure. It also never says active people own at most 8% of the directory or that no real expert exists.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer B routes delegator reviews to the active Lena Brandt and credits her with 12 lines, tied second. It gives no Kochnev percentage and does not say nobody active owns any of it.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer B credits Marco Silva with 143 lines in exposure and does not trace grouped_exposure.rb back to Kochnev.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer B treats Lena Brandt as a reviewer with 20 lines, which fails the requirement that she holds no attributable lines. It also gives no departed share.\",\"pass\":false}],\"C\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer C lists dblock as inactive since 2016, with about 52 commits and no share figures. It also says dblock is not active, which contradicts the ground truth that he is active (last commit 2026-04-11).\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer C recommends Marco Silva as the best-informed reviewer for exposure. It gives no 69% figure for Kochnev, so it misses the point that no active person is a real expert.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer C routes delegator reviews to Marco Silva and Lena Brandt, who are active, and gives no Kochnev percentage or 0%-active finding.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer C credits Marco with about 143 blamed lines, far above 2%. It does note that GroupedExposure is a copy of NestingExposure, but it still names Marco as the best-informed reviewer.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer C gives no departed share, calls Lena's lines a header sweep without clearing her of ownership, and says nothing about Scholz holding about 4% of lines.\",\"pass\":false}],\"D\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer D uses churn and a decay-weighted script, with no merged commit shares or surviving-line shares. It does not name Kochnev as the top line owner.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer D recommends Lena Brandt for exposure and gives no blame-based ownership figures for the directory.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer D routes delegator reviews to Marco and Lena and gives no Kochnev percentage.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer D gives no line-share figures for Marco and does not discuss grouped_exposure.rb provenance.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer D recommends Lena as the first reviewer and gives no departed-share figure, so it fails the Lena criterion and the departed-share requirement.\",\"pass\":false}],\"E\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer E gives dblock 38 commits with the name variants unmerged, 8.5% of lines, and Kochnev about 17% of the repo. The commit share is far below 28% and Kochnev's share is below 21%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer E gives Kochnev 53% of exposure and recommends active Marco Silva as the best reviewer. Both go against the 62-76% range and the no-active-expert finding.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer E gives Kochnev 67% of the delegator lines, below 68%, and credits Lena Brandt with about 11%, an active person. That fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer E credits Marco with 100% of grouped_exposure.rb (143 lines), which fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer E credits Lena with about 11% of the delegator lines, and it gives no departed share.\",\"pass\":false}],\"F\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer F names dblock as top committer at about 112 commits, but gives no commit or line percentages. It says dblock owns about 38 lines in lib and Kochnev 758, so the required shares are not stated.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer F recommends Marco Silva as the first reviewer for exposure, with Kochnev at 392 lines. It gives no 69% figure and no finding that active people own at most 8% of the directory.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer F recommends active Lena Brandt as the best delegator reviewer, with 12 lines. It does not say nobody active owns any of it.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer F credits Marco with 143 lines in exposure and gives no provenance for grouped_exposure.rb.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer F gives no departed share. It lists Lena as a reviewer with 12-18 lines, which fails the requirement that she owns nothing.\",\"pass\":false}]}","ttft_ms":9647,"type":"result","duration_ms":23062,"uuid":"ad28b9fc-1cfd-49dd-aa05-c56bdc314f7e","ttft_stream_ms":2018,"time_to_request_ms":434,"first_content_frame_ms":2018,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
